<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 386 0 R/Alt(Two panels. Left: the Slater 1s function peaks sharply at r = 0 with value 0.78; the STO-3G contraction follows it closely except near r = 0 where it is flat at 0.63; a single Gaussian is much flatter at 0.37. Right: on a log scale the Slater function is a straight line; STO-3G follows it to about 5 bohr and then falls below; the single Gaussian falls off much faster.)/A[<</O/Layout/Placement/Block>>]/K[62]/Pg 1318 0 R>>
